WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.820
Oxygen slips straight
through a cell membrane,

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:05.260
squeezing between its molecules.

3
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.800
A sodium ion is smaller
than an oxygen molecule.

4
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.210
Yet on a bare membrane,
with no proteins at all,

5
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.300
sodium is the slowest of all to cross.

6
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:20.460
So why does oxygen slip through,
while a smaller sodium ion is stopped?

7
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:25.180
In this mission, you'll test five substances
against a bare membrane and see who

8
00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.400
gets through.

9
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:32.140
Then you'll meet channel proteins: gated
pores that let only certain ions through.

10
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:37.420
Your mission: explain why oxygen slips
through a membrane while a smaller sodium

11
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.610
ion is stopped.
